1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:35,730
We're finally back!

2
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:38,830
The air up here is so much better than the dungeons.

3
00:01:39,610 --> 00:01:41,430
Is this sunrise or sunset?

4
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:44,790
Do not touch the window. The spell is still in effect here.

5
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:48,630
Kabro, I'm reporting to the Island Lord tomorrow.

6
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:51,310
I'd like you to join me as a witness.

7
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:53,530
Do you plan on telling him about everything?

8
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:57,290
I don't think it's necessary to mention Laios and his party.

9
00:01:57,290 --> 00:02:01,890
Mostly, I just don't want Fallon to murder anyone else.

10
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:03,550
That makes sense.

11
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:06,050
Why don't you use the rest of the day to get some sleep?

12
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:07,670
Oh! See that, Kuro?

13
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:09,510
Big ship. It's huge.

14
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:12,030
I wonder if the people on it have lots of money!

15
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:18,010
This isn't good.

16
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:22,310
Toshiro, we need to see the Island Lord right away.

17
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,430
Is that ship special?

18
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:26,770
It belongs to the Elves of the West.

19
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:29,090
That bird figurehead.

20
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:31,630
Must be the Canaries, then.

21
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:35,930
They appear when dungeons reach a certain level of danger.

22
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:41,150
When that happens, their mission is to investigate the dungeon and conquer it.

23
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:44,730
I've heard rumors that they've been putting pressure on the Island Lord.

24
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:47,290
But it looks like they're switching to coercion.

25
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:49,750
How is something like that allowed?

26
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:51,870
Isn't this a Tall Man region?

27
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:55,930
To the Elves and Dwarves, races with short lives are like infants.

28
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:59,570
And sadly, the Island Lord is not very good at negotiating.

29
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:01,250
Let's hurry.

30
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:04,990
Huh?

31
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:05,010
Huh?

32
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:06,150
Hey!

33
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:08,510
If it isn't Shuro!

34
00:03:09,050 --> 00:03:09,930
Hello, Nomari.

35
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:11,770
Where's Fallon?

36
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:17,630
Laios and the others haven't given up yet, though.

37
00:03:18,350 --> 00:03:19,010
That's so.

38
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:22,930
They still eating monsters?

39
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,330
Yes, they are.

40
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:27,390
Excuse me, but we're here to see the Island Lord.

41
00:03:27,930 --> 00:03:29,470
Oh, you're out of luck, then.

42
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:32,810
Some important people suddenly came to talk with him.

43
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:35,150
And they've been in there for hours now.

44
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,290
So we're too late.

45
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:38,990
We have to go inside.

46
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:40,390
Is that really wise?

47
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:43,090
If the Elves take control of the dungeon, it's over.

48
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:47,510
The town I'm from also prospered from a dungeon.

49
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:51,850
One day, monsters flooded the town.

50
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:54,070
The Elves came and many died.

51
00:03:55,090 --> 00:03:57,530
Why was my family part of the ones who were killed?

52
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:02,230
My mother was a single parent and did everything she could to raise me.

53
00:04:03,090 --> 00:04:04,850
She didn't deserve to die like that.

54
00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:08,570
I vowed to never let that happen again.

55
00:04:08,570 --> 00:04:12,430
The system in which a single race holds all the power,

56
00:04:12,970 --> 00:04:14,330
it isn't healthy for anyone.

57
00:04:20,810 --> 00:04:24,710
Forgive me, but I've come here to deliver a report to the Island Lord.

58
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:28,390
Excuse me?

59
00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:30,970
As you can see, we're in the middle of something.

60
00:04:31,590 --> 00:04:32,330
Come back later.

61
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:35,210
It's a report about the situation in the dungeon.

62
00:04:35,990 --> 00:04:37,030
Please, hear me out.

63
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:38,550
Seriously?

64
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:40,670
Stand your ground.

65
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:43,990
Make it brief.

66
00:04:44,610 --> 00:04:46,910
Not too long ago, during our exploration,

67
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:49,770
we encountered a human who turned into a monster.

68
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:51,150
What?

69
00:04:52,210 --> 00:04:52,970
Damn it.

70
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:53,790
A chimera.

71
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:55,890
It's progressing faster than expected.

72
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:56,510
See?

73
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:57,770
I told you all!

74
00:04:57,910 --> 00:05:00,590
We didn't have time to twiddle our thumbs and wait for an answer!

75
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:02,370
Let's give the order to make landfall.

76
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:03,610
We won't allow that!

77
00:05:03,610 --> 00:05:05,550
The elderly need not get worked up.

78
00:05:06,150 --> 00:05:09,710
Country borders are so trivial compared to the lives of people.

79
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:13,230
Just who do you think you are, treating me like I'm old and senile?

80
00:05:13,490 --> 00:05:14,530
Tonsu, please.

81
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:15,950
I think we've said enough.

82
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:16,530
What the?

83
00:05:16,530 --> 00:05:20,250
You're a true island lord, understanding and wise.

84
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,470
Now, if you would please stamp here.

85
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:23,170
Don't do it!

86
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:24,510
You can't give in!

87
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:27,630
Did we actually end up making things worse here?

88
00:05:28,230 --> 00:05:29,470
The truth is...

89
00:05:29,470 --> 00:05:32,090
If I had enough strength to conquer a dungeon,

90
00:05:32,690 --> 00:05:33,810
there wouldn't be a problem.

91
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:35,610
But I don't.

92
00:05:36,530 --> 00:05:40,670
So I started looking around for adventurers who were more skilled that I could assist.

93
00:05:42,370 --> 00:05:46,010
However, most of the people I found were self-serving and worthless.

94
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:50,250
By the time I accepted my fate and tried to conquer the dungeon myself,

95
00:05:50,790 --> 00:05:53,290
I heard rumors about the Toten siblings.

96
00:05:53,890 --> 00:05:56,130
I have a feeling that they were brought up pretty well.

97
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:58,890
They have good instincts, but no real ambition.

98
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:00,650
They're honestly kind of weird.

99
00:06:01,690 --> 00:06:04,410
The more I found out, the stranger they seemed.

100
00:06:05,050 --> 00:06:08,770
Despite not being that strong, they reached the deeper floors of the dungeon.

101
00:06:09,330 --> 00:06:11,830
They would give money to people with poor reputations,

102
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:15,490
and their origins in the strange company they kept were hard to follow.

103
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:19,450
Still, there's something about the brother that made me feel

104
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:22,030
he was deeply connected to the destiny of this island.

105
00:06:22,630 --> 00:06:25,770
The question was, would his role be good or bad?

106
00:06:26,130 --> 00:06:29,310
To decide that, I wanted to speak with him directly.

107
00:06:29,710 --> 00:06:31,810
And once I did, I finally understood.

108
00:06:33,150 --> 00:06:35,050
He only thinks about monsters.

109
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:39,390
Therefore, we can't trust him to consider the future of the island.

110
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:41,570
But there's one thing I can say for sure.

111
00:06:41,570 --> 00:06:47,030
At this moment, among the Tall Men, he's the one who's closest to the heart of the dungeon.

112
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:50,750
This will more than likely be the first and last chance we get,

113
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:52,950
so I can't let the elves get in his way.

114
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:56,250
I'll figure out what to do about him after.

115
00:06:57,430 --> 00:06:58,370
Enough already.

116
00:06:58,950 --> 00:07:00,590
You can do whatever you want.

117
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:01,490
My lord!

118
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:02,990
I'll let them know to make landfall.

119
00:07:03,230 --> 00:07:03,870
Please, wait!

120
00:07:04,210 --> 00:07:04,590
Huh?

121
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:06,210
It's too dangerous.

122
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:09,630
The types of monsters, architecture, and environments.

123
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:11,030
All of it's in turmoil.

124
00:07:11,450 --> 00:07:12,870
We're already aware of this.

125
00:07:13,270 --> 00:07:15,410
It's a characteristic of dungeons showing growth.

126
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:17,690
We have to stop it as soon as possible.

127
00:07:18,210 --> 00:07:20,010
In human terms, a growth spurt.

128
00:07:20,570 --> 00:07:22,730
This is when it requires the most nutrients.

129
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:24,070
What's all this now?

130
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,070
About 15 years ago,

131
00:07:27,070 --> 00:07:28,910
a dungeon destroyed my hometown.

132
00:07:28,910 --> 00:07:31,530
It was a town called Utaya.

133
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:33,330
15 years ago?

134
00:07:33,410 --> 00:07:34,470
Then what did that mean?

135
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:35,270
No way!

136
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:37,410
Are you the child they see survived that incident?

137
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:41,330
I did hear that the vice captain or someone had brought a young one home with them.

138
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:42,110
Yes.

139
00:07:42,470 --> 00:07:44,050
They took care of me for several years.

140
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:45,030
Oh?

141
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:48,050
You were probably spoiled, but became an adventurer.

142
00:07:48,450 --> 00:07:51,390
It was my dream to join a squad, but I couldn't as a tall man.

143
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:53,990
I didn't want to repeat that tragedy,

144
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:55,870
so I wanted a way to help.

145
00:07:56,550 --> 00:07:57,430
How admirable.

146
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:59,030
Are you getting enough to eat?

147
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:01,690
You should go and visit the vice captain sometime!

148
00:08:02,070 --> 00:08:02,510
Anyway,

149
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:06,650
you mentioned nutrients.

150
00:08:07,470 --> 00:08:08,130
Tell me more.

151
00:08:09,410 --> 00:08:11,030
Well, because of your efforts,

152
00:08:11,390 --> 00:08:13,230
Utaya's dungeon was quickly destroyed.

153
00:08:13,490 --> 00:08:13,810
However,

154
00:08:14,470 --> 00:08:17,030
there were many casualties among the soldiers and civilians.

155
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:21,590
It was due to the dead turning into monsters and eating the living.

156
00:08:23,210 --> 00:08:25,630
Soldiers were ambushed before they could do anything.

157
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:29,390
Rely on numbers and Utaya will repeat itself.

158
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:31,710
I suggest we seal the dungeon instead.

159
00:08:32,510 --> 00:08:35,050
We can't do anything that will end up feeding it.

160
00:08:35,850 --> 00:08:39,710
I'm pretty sure it's not your intention to cause damage to the dungeon during combat anyway.

161
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:42,110
How many people are inside?

162
00:08:42,430 --> 00:08:44,390
The majority of them are on the first floor.

163
00:08:45,130 --> 00:08:46,610
Let's evacuate them slowly.

164
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:49,290
All humans have some sort of connection.

165
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:52,790
And I know some people who can definitely help out.

166
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:54,850
So just leave it to me!

167
00:08:54,850 --> 00:08:59,470
Cabro,

168
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:03,350
he still ate monsters despite everything he went through?

169
00:09:06,110 --> 00:09:07,390
Begin preparations

170
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:09,810
for the investigation.

171
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:10,330
Huh?

172
00:09:10,330 --> 00:09:13,910
I suspect you're plotting something.

173
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:15,650
If that's the case,

174
00:09:15,890 --> 00:09:16,950
show me what you've got.

175
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:19,090
Should anything go wrong,

176
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:20,830
my troops will rush in.

177
00:09:21,750 --> 00:09:22,170
Understood.

178
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:23,570
Yes.

179
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:34,330
So are they like scrambled eggs?

180
00:09:34,790 --> 00:09:35,090
Huh?

181
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:38,610
You said before that people compare souls to eggs.

182
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:41,590
But if you're referring to souls that are mixed together,

183
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:44,270
then what would that mean in relation to how eggs are cooked?

184
00:09:44,990 --> 00:09:45,670
For example,

185
00:09:45,930 --> 00:09:46,690
scrambled eggs,

186
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:48,050
a sunny-side-up egg,

187
00:09:48,070 --> 00:09:48,890
and a poached egg

188
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:50,490
would all have different stories.

189
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:51,690
Listen, Senshi.

190
00:09:51,950 --> 00:09:53,230
I didn't make that comparison

191
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:54,510
for you to take what I said

192
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:56,010
and try to make a joke out of it.

193
00:09:56,330 --> 00:09:57,330
Who's making jokes?

194
00:09:57,850 --> 00:09:58,990
I was actually impressed

195
00:09:58,990 --> 00:10:00,870
by how interesting a comparison it was.

196
00:10:01,690 --> 00:10:03,290
There's nothing else that behaves

197
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:05,310
in as many different ways as an egg does.

198
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:06,350
For example,

199
00:10:06,590 --> 00:10:07,990
eggs get firm when heated,

200
00:10:08,230 --> 00:10:09,810
but the white and yolk solidify

201
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:10,870
at different temperatures.

202
00:10:11,370 --> 00:10:11,830
Frothiness,

203
00:10:12,090 --> 00:10:12,850
moisture retention,

204
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:13,610
viscosity,

205
00:10:14,310 --> 00:10:15,790
and the most interesting one,

206
00:10:16,370 --> 00:10:17,270
emulsification.

207
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:19,630
Even things that don't mix naturally

208
00:10:19,630 --> 00:10:20,810
like oil and water

209
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:21,790
mixed beautifully

210
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:22,910
under the right conditions.

211
00:10:23,310 --> 00:10:24,610
Just like this.

212
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:25,630
Well, that's...

213
00:10:26,490 --> 00:10:28,530
Wait, souls are actually nothing like eggs.

214
00:10:29,090 --> 00:10:29,570
Laios,

215
00:10:29,730 --> 00:10:31,110
you mind handing me that bread there?

216
00:10:42,470 --> 00:10:43,370
It's ready.

217
00:10:43,370 --> 00:10:49,750
So, how are we supposed to eat this?

218
00:10:50,130 --> 00:10:51,930
Pick up the bread with your knife and fork,

219
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:54,590
then use the bread to scoop the yolk and sauce

220
00:10:54,590 --> 00:10:55,090
as you eat.

221
00:11:01,090 --> 00:11:02,750
Delicious as usual.

222
00:11:04,190 --> 00:11:06,450
If you don't mind,

223
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:08,470
could you stop looking around at stuff

224
00:11:08,470 --> 00:11:09,470
that isn't really there?

225
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:10,810
Or is there something?

226
00:11:11,350 --> 00:11:12,370
I don't think so.

227
00:11:12,810 --> 00:11:14,850
I just thought I felt some kind of presence.

228
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:15,490
Huh?

229
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:19,370
Does that mean this isn't a hallucination?

230
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:21,150
Huh?

231
00:11:23,170 --> 00:11:25,310
Well, when I'd gotten mana sickness,

232
00:11:25,790 --> 00:11:26,770
remember when I mentioned

233
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:28,290
I was seeing and hearing things?

234
00:11:28,650 --> 00:11:30,330
That never went away.

235
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:31,070
Seriously?

236
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:32,410
Why didn't you say something?

237
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:34,350
Because Chill would just yell at me

238
00:11:34,350 --> 00:11:35,550
and tell me I'm sick in the head.

239
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:36,810
That's because you are.

240
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:39,370
What are you hallucinating?

241
00:11:39,370 --> 00:11:43,790
Day in and day out,

242
00:11:43,930 --> 00:11:45,490
something keeps trying to talk to me.

243
00:11:45,950 --> 00:11:48,070
At first, I couldn't tell what it was saying.

244
00:11:48,830 --> 00:11:49,790
But gradually,

245
00:11:49,970 --> 00:11:51,950
its voice and shape started getting clearer.

246
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:53,370
It's pretty scary,

247
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:55,350
so I've been pretending not to see it.

248
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,830
Then you could actually hear me speaking after all.

249
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:01,330
So what did it say?

250
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:04,530
Well, it's not too happy that I was ignoring it.

251
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:06,710
I wonder if talking to it is okay.

252
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:07,950
Do you think it's evil?

253
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:09,610
Uh, not sure.

254
00:12:10,410 --> 00:12:10,730
Possibly.

255
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:13,130
Hello there!

256
00:12:13,510 --> 00:12:14,690
Can I help you with something?

257
00:12:15,650 --> 00:12:15,990
Uh-huh.

258
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:18,650
What's it saying now?

259
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:22,230
It's mad at me because I thought it was an evil ghost.

260
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:23,530
Also,

261
00:12:23,950 --> 00:12:26,190
it's asking if we've forgotten

262
00:12:26,190 --> 00:12:28,330
that it saved us from the, uh, mage.

263
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:29,150
Huh?

264
00:12:29,150 --> 00:12:31,230
Oh, wait!

265
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:32,070
I remember!

266
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:33,190
Right.

267
00:12:33,330 --> 00:12:34,790
How could I forget that whole thing?

268
00:12:35,070 --> 00:12:36,310
Please give it our thanks.

269
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:37,030
Hmm.

270
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:37,770
Mm-hmm.

271
00:12:38,190 --> 00:12:40,230
I guess it wants to introduce us to someone?

272
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:41,410
Thoughts?

273
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:43,550
It's not the god of death, is it?

274
00:12:43,690 --> 00:12:44,130
Well,

275
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,210
we don't have many options, so...

276
00:12:46,210 --> 00:12:46,670
All right.

277
00:12:47,050 --> 00:12:48,990
We're ready to go whenever you are.

278
00:12:48,990 --> 00:13:18,970
We're ready to go whenever you are.

279
00:13:19,690 --> 00:13:20,370
Oh!

280
00:13:25,970 --> 00:13:26,610
What?

281
00:13:27,610 --> 00:13:28,290
Wait.

282
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:29,590
What the heck?

283
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:31,170
Where are we?

284
00:13:31,570 --> 00:13:31,890
Hey!

285
00:13:33,190 --> 00:13:34,910
Out of the road, please!

286
00:13:35,430 --> 00:13:37,330
Is that a unicorn?

287
00:13:39,490 --> 00:13:40,650
That clothing.

288
00:13:41,050 --> 00:13:42,430
Did you guys come from the outside?

289
00:13:42,850 --> 00:13:43,270
No.

290
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,430
We came from the dungeon and...

291
00:13:45,430 --> 00:13:46,630
I can't believe it.

292
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:47,790
Come with me.

293
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:58,010
I've never seen monsters be this docile before.

294
00:13:58,350 --> 00:14:00,110
It's because they're ordered not to hurt us,

295
00:14:00,170 --> 00:14:01,530
so we can coexist here.

296
00:14:01,830 --> 00:14:02,270
Whoa.

297
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:04,750
That's not going to be the case for outsiders, though.

298
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:07,390
So make sure you hold on to the stuff I gave you.

299
00:14:08,950 --> 00:14:09,430
Izutsumi?

300
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:10,590
Something wrong?

301
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:12,310
Teleportation sickness?

302
00:14:12,630 --> 00:14:13,890
She's probably tired.

303
00:14:13,890 --> 00:14:17,310
Is that the Golden Castle?

304
00:14:17,610 --> 00:14:18,290
Sure is.

305
00:14:18,850 --> 00:14:21,090
And the ghosts that brought us to this place,

306
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:23,270
are they actual residents, too?

307
00:14:23,490 --> 00:14:24,290
Pretty much.

308
00:14:24,710 --> 00:14:25,090
Well,

309
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:27,550
the person you're about to meet has more info.

310
00:14:28,230 --> 00:14:29,810
Maybe they'll know why you were chosen,

311
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:31,110
because we sure don't.

312
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:32,790
We were chosen?

313
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:35,410
This is it.

314
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:36,630
Just sit tight, okay?

315
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:41,130
If you're looking for the master,

316
00:14:41,350 --> 00:14:42,330
he went to the church.

317
00:14:44,830 --> 00:14:45,570
It's them.

318
00:14:46,070 --> 00:14:46,310
Huh?

319
00:14:46,950 --> 00:14:47,730
Those guys?

320
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:51,330
Guess we came here at a pretty bad time.

321
00:14:51,990 --> 00:14:53,670
Until the master comes back here,

322
00:14:53,850 --> 00:14:55,610
why don't you try to relax in the village?

323
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:58,410
Seems like everyone really wants to show you

324
00:14:58,410 --> 00:14:59,110
their hospitality.

325
00:14:59,890 --> 00:15:02,150
What should we take them around to see first?

326
00:15:02,370 --> 00:15:04,550
The village isn't that special, so...

327
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:06,410
They're all residents of the Golden Castle?

328
00:15:06,790 --> 00:15:08,510
Yeah, but I don't see any old folk.

329
00:15:09,210 --> 00:15:10,450
Honestly, I'd like to see

330
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:11,970
where the monsters are being raised.

331
00:15:12,210 --> 00:15:12,450
Huh?

332
00:15:12,970 --> 00:15:14,730
I want to take a tour of the fields

333
00:15:14,730 --> 00:15:15,910
we saw on the way over.

334
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:16,870
Huh?

335
00:15:17,070 --> 00:15:18,510
That's what you're interested in?

336
00:15:18,510 --> 00:15:20,550
I mean, that's easy enough.

337
00:15:20,970 --> 00:15:21,490
Hooray!

338
00:15:23,250 --> 00:15:25,310
I'll just wait for them to get back.

339
00:15:25,610 --> 00:15:27,630
Can't leave he's a tsumi alone anyway.

340
00:15:27,890 --> 00:15:28,750
I agree.

341
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:31,170
That's a minotaur!

342
00:15:31,370 --> 00:15:32,630
And it's female!

343
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:35,890
We milk this instead of cows.

344
00:15:36,110 --> 00:15:37,430
Why are you raising monsters?

345
00:15:37,990 --> 00:15:39,730
Oh, because normal livestock

346
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:41,090
was hard to get a hold of.

347
00:15:41,090 --> 00:15:41,610
Oh!

348
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:45,250
Oh!

349
00:15:49,790 --> 00:15:52,150
What a beautiful field.

350
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:53,950
It's so well tended to.

351
00:15:53,950 --> 00:15:56,850
Is everything here used up by the villagers?

352
00:15:57,370 --> 00:15:59,470
We admittedly waste quite a lot of it.

353
00:15:59,890 --> 00:16:01,930
But if we didn't have fields to keep us busy,

354
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:02,950
we'd have nothing to do.

355
00:16:03,430 --> 00:16:04,710
It's mostly an appearance,

356
00:16:04,970 --> 00:16:06,750
but we try to mimic surface life.

357
00:16:07,010 --> 00:16:07,410
Really?

358
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:11,930
Isutsumi, are you okay?

359
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:17,190
At least she doesn't seem sick, I guess.

360
00:16:18,830 --> 00:16:19,270
Sorry!

361
00:16:19,490 --> 00:16:21,410
We don't mean to interrupt, but...

362
00:16:21,970 --> 00:16:23,570
Dresses?

363
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:25,350
Exactly!

364
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:27,350
They're dresses we made by hand.

365
00:16:27,430 --> 00:16:29,530
We've gotten so bored of modeling them ourselves.

366
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:31,930
We need the fresh face of an outsider to do it.

367
00:16:31,930 --> 00:16:33,630
Sure, if you want me to.

368
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:36,290
Which should we try?

369
00:16:36,490 --> 00:16:37,910
It has to be the red one!

370
00:16:38,090 --> 00:16:39,190
You'll have to forgive us.

371
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:41,610
Our dresses might seem a little old-fashioned

372
00:16:41,610 --> 00:16:42,490
from your perspective.

373
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:44,170
I'm sure it's fine.

374
00:16:48,490 --> 00:16:51,050
Somehow this is different than what I expected.

375
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:53,170
Guess this is what happens

376
00:16:53,170 --> 00:16:55,370
when you've been isolated for a thousand years.

377
00:16:55,370 --> 00:16:56,970
Try this on next!

378
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:01,650
This is great!

379
00:17:02,010 --> 00:17:03,990
I'm pretty picky about my alcohol,

380
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:05,570
but this isn't bad at all.

381
00:17:05,870 --> 00:17:06,630
Happy to hear.

382
00:17:06,970 --> 00:17:08,690
I've been serving it to my Orc customers,

383
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:11,770
and this recent batch is really popular among them.

384
00:17:13,250 --> 00:17:14,310
Yeah, I bet.

385
00:17:14,650 --> 00:17:15,750
Oh, what about wine?

386
00:17:15,870 --> 00:17:16,670
Do you make that?

387
00:17:16,990 --> 00:17:17,710
Well, I do,

388
00:17:17,830 --> 00:17:19,490
but it's much newer than making ale.

389
00:17:19,490 --> 00:17:21,650
Been doing that 400 years now,

390
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,430
so making the switch has been tricky.

391
00:17:23,630 --> 00:17:24,810
That long, huh?

392
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:26,430
Sounds pretty established.

393
00:17:26,790 --> 00:17:28,030
What generation are you?

394
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,830
I started it when I was 600,

395
00:17:30,070 --> 00:17:31,110
so first generation.

396
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:32,890
Come again?

397
00:17:34,590 --> 00:17:35,650
Chilchuk, guess what?

398
00:17:35,690 --> 00:17:37,090
They let me milk a minotaur!

399
00:17:37,410 --> 00:17:38,550
Hey, good for you.

400
00:17:38,670 --> 00:17:40,170
Keep that to yourself next time.

401
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:41,650
This place is incredible!

402
00:17:42,130 --> 00:17:44,730
They've completely succeeded in cultivating monsters

403
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:45,690
and made it an art!

404
00:17:46,070 --> 00:17:46,830
Do you see that?

405
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:49,470
It's the biggest dryad garden I've ever seen!

406
00:17:49,930 --> 00:17:51,810
The minotaur had four nipples like a cow!

407
00:17:52,390 --> 00:17:54,450
I'm not feeling so good.

408
00:17:54,810 --> 00:17:57,730
That was a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

409
00:17:57,990 --> 00:17:59,070
You really missed out?

410
00:17:59,570 --> 00:18:00,230
By the way,

411
00:18:00,490 --> 00:18:01,610
where did the other two go?

412
00:18:02,070 --> 00:18:03,790
What's with the weird non-sequitur?

413
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:06,010
Uh, we're over here.

414
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:12,470
What in the hell are you wearing?

415
00:18:12,610 --> 00:18:13,690
Playing dress-up, huh?

416
00:18:13,690 --> 00:18:14,490
Don't misunderstand!

417
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:16,490
I was asked to wear this, I swear!

418
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:20,490
I actually, this was the tamest one I tried on.

419
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:23,370
Marcelle, you, uh...

420
00:18:24,110 --> 00:18:25,170
Uh, yeah?

421
00:18:25,590 --> 00:18:26,050
Lyos?

422
00:18:28,010 --> 00:18:30,530
You have any clue why she's stuck to you like that?

423
00:18:30,770 --> 00:18:31,910
Oh, that, right!

424
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:33,410
Yeah, I have no idea!

425
00:18:33,550 --> 00:18:34,230
That's so weird!

426
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:38,230
Uh, it's like she switched brains with a child or something!

427
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:39,050
Uh!

428
00:18:39,410 --> 00:18:39,910
Oh!

429
00:18:40,910 --> 00:18:41,110
Yeah!

430
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:45,350
Lots of barriers have been cast here in many different layers.

431
00:18:45,730 --> 00:18:48,930
And it seems like it's affecting Izutsumi in some way.

432
00:18:49,470 --> 00:18:51,350
It's because she's half-monster, right?

433
00:18:51,650 --> 00:18:51,990
Yeah.

434
00:18:52,710 --> 00:18:56,550
But I've never seen a barrier make monsters non-aggressive before.

435
00:18:57,690 --> 00:19:00,070
I really wish I could decipher this.

436
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:02,570
But I don't know most of these characters,

437
00:19:02,730 --> 00:19:04,010
and I don't have time to learn!

438
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:07,650
Why the hell do these things have to be so hard to read and secretive?

439
00:19:08,310 --> 00:19:11,150
Anyway, this really is an amazing place.

440
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:13,350
Under different circumstances,

441
00:19:13,750 --> 00:19:15,690
I wouldn't mind staying here forever.

442
00:19:17,410 --> 00:19:18,350
Same here.

443
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:26,250
My apologies for the long wait.

444
00:19:26,650 --> 00:19:27,410
It isn't much,

445
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:29,450
but we've prepared a warm meal for all of you.

446
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:30,670
This way, please.

447
00:19:35,230 --> 00:19:36,770
Ah, welcome, everyone.

448
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:38,470
I've been wanting to meet you.

449
00:19:38,950 --> 00:19:39,550
I'm Yod.

450
00:19:39,650 --> 00:19:40,290
It's a pleasure.

451
00:19:40,870 --> 00:19:42,630
You already know of Delgol, yes?

452
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:44,210
Well, he's my grandfather.

453
00:19:45,070 --> 00:19:45,590
Delgol?

454
00:19:45,830 --> 00:19:47,490
Please, feel free to take a seat.

455
00:19:48,190 --> 00:19:50,090
You're wondering why I've called you here.

456
00:19:50,090 --> 00:19:52,410
This will take some time to explain.

457
00:19:53,290 --> 00:19:54,290
Let's see it first.

458
00:20:00,890 --> 00:20:02,830
Uh, is this meat?

459
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:03,510
Yes!

460
00:20:03,730 --> 00:20:05,670
As your party had specifically requested,

461
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:07,590
we prepared Minotaur meat!

462
00:20:07,590 --> 00:20:12,870
Does everyone in the village routinely eat monsters, too?

463
00:20:13,410 --> 00:20:14,550
There are some who do,

464
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:17,170
although we don't really need to consume food.

465
00:20:17,430 --> 00:20:17,710
Huh?

466
00:20:18,070 --> 00:20:20,650
Our sense of taste has completely dulled.

467
00:20:21,170 --> 00:20:21,990
Aside from that,

468
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:24,150
we have no real appetite to speak of.

469
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:26,910
Such is the curse of immortality

470
00:20:26,910 --> 00:20:30,010
that the mad mage cast on the people of this village.

471
00:20:30,010 --> 00:20:35,110
Do you know why the mage would do something like that?

472
00:20:35,390 --> 00:20:35,710
No.

473
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:38,430
When I grew old enough to know what was happening,

474
00:20:38,910 --> 00:20:40,310
the mage was already in a state

475
00:20:40,310 --> 00:20:42,370
where communicating with him was difficult.

476
00:20:43,870 --> 00:20:46,410
But please, don't let our problems stop you.

477
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,050
Go eat up to your heart's content.

478
00:20:48,690 --> 00:20:49,790
We may not get hungry,

479
00:20:50,130 --> 00:20:52,130
but simply being able to watch others eat

480
00:20:52,130 --> 00:20:53,270
still brings us joy.

481
00:20:53,270 --> 00:20:55,630
Well, now, I definitely can't say

482
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:57,350
that I don't really want to eat this.

483
00:21:00,910 --> 00:21:01,350
Grandfather.

484
00:21:02,190 --> 00:21:03,970
For as long as I can remember,

485
00:21:04,570 --> 00:21:05,930
he always blamed himself

486
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:07,930
for being the one who made the mad mage

487
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:09,750
become obsessed with black magic.

488
00:21:10,250 --> 00:21:11,690
So in order to look for help,

489
00:21:11,970 --> 00:21:13,070
he headed to the surface.

490
00:21:15,410 --> 00:21:16,330
Perhaps you know.

491
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:17,750
How did he fare up there?

492
00:21:18,150 --> 00:21:19,650
Well, from what I've heard,

493
00:21:19,650 --> 00:21:22,490
he was seen emerging from the underground cemetery.

494
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:25,190
He claimed he was the king of a ruined country

495
00:21:25,190 --> 00:21:26,870
and would give his entire kingdom

496
00:21:26,870 --> 00:21:29,010
to the one who defeated the mad mage,

497
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:30,410
then turn to dust.

498
00:21:31,170 --> 00:21:32,090
Is that so?

499
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:35,190
He's finally been released from his agony.

500
00:21:35,810 --> 00:21:37,430
Knowing this brings me solace.

501
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:40,370
Many people have attempted to escape the curse

502
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:41,590
by leaving the village.

503
00:21:42,230 --> 00:21:43,690
However, none have succeeded

504
00:21:43,690 --> 00:21:46,330
and their physical bodies are lost as a result.

505
00:21:47,330 --> 00:21:50,230
Without a body, you gradually lose yourself,

506
00:21:50,590 --> 00:21:51,870
become an evil ghost,

507
00:21:51,870 --> 00:21:54,390
and then are unable to return here.

508
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:57,390
I'm sure you've encountered these ghosts before.

509
00:21:57,830 --> 00:21:58,190
Yeah.

510
00:21:58,710 --> 00:22:00,550
We attacked them with holy water

511
00:22:00,550 --> 00:22:02,230
and then made us for a bay out of them.

512
00:22:03,190 --> 00:22:04,550
So, anyway,

513
00:22:05,030 --> 00:22:07,530
you never told us why we were called to this place.

514
00:22:07,870 --> 00:22:08,530
The prophecy.

515
00:22:09,070 --> 00:22:09,630
Prophecy?

516
00:22:10,150 --> 00:22:10,570
Indeed.

517
00:22:11,250 --> 00:22:12,730
One shall arrive at the village

518
00:22:12,730 --> 00:22:14,350
with winged sword in hand.

519
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:15,870
They will be the hero

520
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,570
who will defeat the mad mage

521
00:22:17,570 --> 00:22:18,790
and set us all free.

522
00:22:19,230 --> 00:22:20,030
Winged sword.

523
00:22:20,190 --> 00:22:21,330
Does he mean Kensuke?

524
00:22:21,650 --> 00:22:23,530
Well, there are wings on it, although...

525
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:24,910
Wait!

526
00:22:25,090 --> 00:22:26,950
This lion face wasn't on here before!

527
00:22:27,390 --> 00:22:28,530
When did...

528
00:22:28,530 --> 00:22:32,050
The winged lion is our guardian deity.

529
00:22:32,050 --> 00:22:35,170
He was imprisoned at the very bottom of the dungeon

530
00:22:35,170 --> 00:22:36,390
by the mad mage.

531
00:22:36,910 --> 00:22:37,250
However,

532
00:22:37,570 --> 00:22:39,270
the lion still guides us

533
00:22:39,270 --> 00:22:40,530
by telling us prophecies

534
00:22:40,530 --> 00:22:41,750
by way of our dreams.

535
00:22:42,430 --> 00:22:44,090
And those prophecies are why

536
00:22:44,090 --> 00:22:46,110
my grandfather left for the surface.

537
00:22:46,110 --> 00:22:48,670
Sir Laios,

538
00:22:48,790 --> 00:22:50,670
there is more to the prophecy.

539
00:22:51,630 --> 00:22:53,570
With the winged sword in their hand,

540
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:56,190
the hero will defeat the mad mage

541
00:22:56,190 --> 00:22:59,390
and thus rise as the country's new king.

542
00:23:00,390 --> 00:23:00,910
Wait!

543
00:23:01,070 --> 00:23:02,110
You can't be serious!

544
00:23:02,290 --> 00:23:04,570
He just picked up that sword by complete accident!

545
00:23:04,730 --> 00:23:05,790
It was no accident.

546
00:23:06,530 --> 00:23:08,770
The fact the sword is in this room with us

547
00:23:08,770 --> 00:23:10,530
means it was something preordained.

548
00:23:12,890 --> 00:23:14,170
Now, Sir Laios,

549
00:23:14,170 --> 00:23:16,710
can you please promise me something?

550
00:23:17,770 --> 00:23:19,790
Promise me you'll defeat the mad mage

551
00:23:19,790 --> 00:23:22,050
and free everyone in this village!

552
00:23:23,050 --> 00:23:24,910
But I...

553
00:23:24,910 --> 00:23:33,210
Can you please let me think about it?

554
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:35,670
You gotta turn him down.

555
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:37,870
Why bother giving them hope like that?

556
00:23:38,210 --> 00:23:40,210
Because I can't flat-out refuse.

557
00:23:40,930 --> 00:23:41,410
Kensuke,

558
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:43,570
when'd you even get like this?

559
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:44,150
Huh, buddy?

560
00:23:45,110 --> 00:23:46,510
Maybe it was when you got eaten

561
00:23:46,510 --> 00:23:47,810
by the dungeon cleaners.

562
00:23:49,950 --> 00:23:52,370
I was actually so nervous during all that,

563
00:23:52,570 --> 00:23:54,450
I couldn't really taste any of the food

564
00:23:54,450 --> 00:23:55,350
they made for us.

565
00:23:55,890 --> 00:23:57,690
You've got some nerve, you know that?

566
00:23:57,910 --> 00:24:00,050
Specifically requested by the party, huh?

567
00:24:00,850 --> 00:24:02,710
It really didn't have that much flavor

568
00:24:02,710 --> 00:24:03,530
to begin with.

569
00:24:03,950 --> 00:24:04,350
Huh?

570
00:24:04,590 --> 00:24:05,870
You said they have no appetite,

571
00:24:06,110 --> 00:24:07,330
so they don't need to eat anything.

572
00:24:08,050 --> 00:24:09,530
I think it's safe to assume

573
00:24:09,530 --> 00:24:11,230
that's why they're not very good at cooking.

574
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:13,910
I just realized something.

575
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:16,070
The people in this village,

576
00:24:16,250 --> 00:24:18,130
they don't really need to tend fields

577
00:24:18,130 --> 00:24:19,090
and use dishware,

578
00:24:19,250 --> 00:24:20,950
so why bother keeping them around?

579
00:24:21,550 --> 00:24:23,590
What was the point in wasting all that energy

580
00:24:23,590 --> 00:24:25,150
to continue maintaining them

581
00:24:25,150 --> 00:24:26,950
for the last thousand years or so?

582
00:24:26,950 --> 00:24:30,730
I reckon it's because they actually do need those things.

583
00:24:31,230 --> 00:24:32,990
It helps them keep their sanity

584
00:24:32,990 --> 00:24:35,310
and gives them a reason to live.

585
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:37,590
Laios,

586
00:24:37,830 --> 00:24:40,950
when we were with the Orc Chief on the third floor,

587
00:24:41,450 --> 00:24:43,890
I still remember exactly what you told them.

588
00:24:43,890 --> 00:24:47,650
What did I say again?

589
00:24:48,030 --> 00:24:48,350
Well,

590
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:51,070
make sure you take the night to think about it.

591
00:24:53,370 --> 00:24:55,450
Do you mind if I sleep in here, too?

592
00:24:55,590 --> 00:24:57,290
Go sleep in the room they gave you.

593
00:24:57,550 --> 00:24:59,330
But I don't want to be alone in there.

594
00:24:59,590 --> 00:25:01,130
And Izutsumi's being weird.

595
00:25:01,470 --> 00:25:02,490
Come on, scoot over.

596
00:25:02,610 --> 00:25:03,670
Just sleep on the floor.

597
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,470
His hands were so cold.

598
00:25:06,470 --> 00:25:36,450
I don't want to be alone in there.

